# specbench — line ending policy
#
# The benchmark scripts run on Windows and write their JSON and JSONL results
# with CRLF, while the same files were committed with LF. Git then reports
# every results file as wholly rewritten whenever a run finishes, which buries
# the one or two files that genuinely changed under several thousand lines of
# noise and makes it impossible to review a run's output by reading a diff.
#
# `text=auto` normalises text files to LF in the repository while leaving the
# working tree alone, so a CRLF file on disk and an LF file in the index are
# understood to be the same file.
* text=auto

# Binary formats, listed explicitly rather than left to auto-detection. A
# false positive here would corrupt the file on checkout.
*.docx binary
*.pt   binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf  binary
*.safetensors binary
